From 7c089fad0e66e4e56e439fcfa598e9ab4c035efe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:08:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93 - lower DMA buffer thresholds to 64 bytes

The default 128-byte output threshold can intermittently corrupt the
final partial word of authenc plaintext on Airoha EN7581, even after
successful authentication. Output thresholds below 128 avoid the observed
failure, while lowering only the input threshold does not. Reducing the
DMA maximum burst setting also avoids the failure but costs throughput.

Program 64-byte input and output thresholds for all EIP93 devices. This
writes 0x00400040 to PE_BUF_THRESH and keeps the output threshold below
the observed failure boundary. Device throughput measurements did not
change across output thresholds of 32, 64, 96 and 124.

Retain the existing DMA burst setting, alignment checks and authenc
fallbacks. This does not establish that unaligned source DMA is reliable.

Signed-off-by: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
---
 eip93-main.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/eip93-main.c b/eip93-main.c
index a8e9632..b5d9846 100644
--- a/eip93-main.c
+++ b/eip93-main.c
@@ -367,9 +367,9 @@ static void eip93_initialize(struct eip93_device *eip93, u32 supported_algo_flag
 
 	eip93_configure_dma(eip93);
 
-	/* Config DMA thresholds */
-	val = FIELD_PREP(EIP93_PE_OUTBUF_THRESH, 128) |
-	      FIELD_PREP(EIP93_PE_INBUF_THRESH, 128);
+	/* Keep DMA thresholds below the size that corrupts Airoha output tails. */
+	val = FIELD_PREP(EIP93_PE_OUTBUF_THRESH, 64) |
+	      FIELD_PREP(EIP93_PE_INBUF_THRESH, 64);
 	writel(val, eip93->base + EIP93_REG_PE_BUF_THRESH);
 
 	/* Clear/ack all interrupts before disable all */
